Text:
fearlessManager is a program.
The 'single' manager is the fearlessManager that holds the lock of the LockFile "single_manager_at_" Port ".lock" of the ManagerFolder, and listens on Port.
The 'single' manager receives the messages that fearlessMessage sends, one at a time.
A 'ManagerFolder' is a folder holding one file with a name of form LockFile, the file projects.info, and the folders icons and locks.
The 'manager path' is the path of the ManagerFolder.
fearlessManager, run with no parameters, and fearlessMessage, run with one Message, deduce the same 'manager path'.
The folder locks holds the files that show which mounted data a running project uses.
projects.info is a file containing an Info serialized as defined in the fearless standard library; only fearlessManager writes projects.info.
Infos.msg(""), Infos.list() and Infos.map() are one Info, the empty Info.
The errors messageErrorNameNotAssociatedWithBase16(ProjectName,Base16), messageErrorNameNotAssociatedWithAnyRegisteredProject(ProjectName), messageErrorBase16NotAssociatedWithAnyRegisteredProject(Base16), messageErrorNoInfoInFileAtBase16(Base16), messageErrorNewMetadataIsNotValid(Info) and internalErrorCanNotAddMessageToFullQueue(Message) are left unspecified in the design.
Info[..] makes a new Info with a little difference; for example ProjectsInfo[+=Project] makes a new Info where the list contains also that Project.
Info."key" is the Info that the key "key" maps to in the Infos.map Info; for example Project."path" is the Infos.msg holding the TaggedText of Project.
Message[Target=Target'] makes a new Message where Target is replaced by Target'.
fearlessManager.projectsInfo is a ProjectsInfo held in memory; fearlessManager.projectsInfo starts as Infos.list().
fearlessManager.names is a Names held in memory; fearlessManager.names starts as {}.
fearlessManager.queue is a Queue held in memory; fearlessManager.queue starts empty.
The 'queue limit' is the maximum number of Messages of a Queue.

Grammar:
ProjectsInfo ::= Infos.list(Project1 .. Projectn)
TypeNames ::= Infos.list(Infos.msg(TypeName1) .. Infos.msg(TypeNamen))
Project ::= Infos.map("path", Infos.msg(TaggedText), "kind", Infos.msg(Kind), "mains", TypeNames, "mounts", Mount, "attenuators", Attenuator)
Mount ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, Infos.msg(ProjectName1) .. TypeNamen, Infos.msg(ProjectNamen))
Attenuator ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, TypeNames1 .. TypeNamen, TypeNamesn)
Kind ::= "idle" | "code" | "dataRead" | "dataEdit"
ProjectName ::= [a-z_][a-z0-9_]*
TaggedText ::= \
  Base16                                 \
  | "Str:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn \
  | "UStr:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn
EscapedChar ::= [0-9A-Za-z+\-*/=<>,.;:()\[\]{}`'!?@#$%^&_|~\\] | "\"" | " "
Names ::= (TaggedText1->ProjectName1) .. (TaggedTextn->ProjectNamen)
TypeName ::= PackageName "." TypeBaseName
PackageName ::= [a-z][a-z0-9_]*
TypeBaseName ::= [_]*[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*[']*
ValidSegment ::= SegmentBase | SegmentBase "." OSExtension | SegmentBase "." MultiExtension
SegmentBase ::= [a-z_][a-z0-9_]{0,190}
OSExtension ::= [a-z0-9]{1,16}
MultiExtension ::= "css.map" | "d.ts" | "d.ts.map" | "js.map" | "min.css" | "min.js" | "tar.bz2" | "tar.gz" | "tar.lz" | "tar.lz4" | "tar.xz" | "tar.zst"
ReservedName ::= "con" | "prn" | "aux" | "nul" | "com" [1-9] | "lpt" [1-9]
Info ::= Infos.msg(Str) | Infos.list(Info1 .. Infon) | Infos.map(Str1, Info1 .. Strn, Infon)
LockFile ::= "no_manager.lock" | "candidate_manager.lock" | "single_manager_at_" Port ".lock"
Port ::= [1-9][0-9]*
Queue ::= "\t" Message1 "\n" .. "\t" Messagen "\n"

Well formedness:
in Queue: n is at most the 'queue limit'
in ProjectsInfo: Project1."path" .. Projectn."path" are disjoint
in Project: Project."mains" is Infos.list(Infos.msg(TypeName1) .. Infos.msg(TypeNamen)) with TypeName1 .. TypeNamen disjoint
in ProjectName: ProjectName ".fearless" is of form ValidSegment
in TaggedText: if TaggedText is "Str:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn, then EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn is the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless Str encoding a valid OS FS path
in TaggedText: if TaggedText is "UStr:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn, then EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn is the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless UStr encoding a valid OS FS path, and p.isStr is False
in TaggedText: TaggedText is of form Base16 only if no Fearless UStr encodes the path that TaggedText decodes to
in PackageName: PackageName is not of form ReservedName
in SegmentBase: SegmentBase is not of form ReservedName
in Info: if Info is Infos.map(Str1, Info1 .. Strn, Infon), then Str1 .. Strn are disjoint
in Port: Port is a number smaller than 65536

Notation: Base16.taggedText = TaggedText where:
- Base16 and TaggedText encode the same path

Notation: ProjectName.resolve(Names) = Base16 where:
- Names = Names1 (Base16.taggedText->ProjectName) Names2
- no pair of Names1 Names2 maps a key to ProjectName

Notation: ProjectsInfo.get(Base16) = Project where:
- Project in ProjectsInfo
- Project."path" = Infos.msg(Base16.taggedText)

Define fearlessManager$writeProjectsInfo():
A action fearlessManager replaces projects.info with fearlessManager.projectsInfo serialized
B action fearlessManager tells the manager GUI, if the manager GUI runs, to read projects.info again

Define fearlessManager$readName(Infos.msg(TaggedText)):
A if the folder at TaggedText has the name ProjectName, return (TaggedText->ProjectName)
B action return {}

Define fearlessManager$refreshCachedNames():
A fact fearlessManager.projectsInfo = Infos.list(Project1 .. Projectn)
B action fearlessManager.names= fearlessManager$readName(Project1."path") .. fearlessManager$readName(Projectn."path")

Invariant:
At every moment, at most one fearlessManager is the 'single' manager of one ManagerFolder.

Define fearlessManager$serve():
A fact fearlessManager holds the lock of no_manager.lock.
B action fearlessManager renames no_manager.lock to candidate_manager.lock
C action fearlessManager listens for connections on the loopback address, on the port Port that the OS picks
//later: copy the icons, Coordinator$dropUnfinished, buildMap, show the tray icon
D action fearlessManager renames candidate_manager.lock to "single_manager_at_" Port ".lock"
E after fearlessManager is the 'single' manager.

Story:
A event fearlessManager starts.
B fact At least one file of the folder at the 'manager path' has a name of form LockFile, and no process holds the lock of any of those files.
C action fearlessManager takes the lock of each of those files
D action fearlessManager deletes all of those files but one, and renames that one to no_manager.lock
E action fearlessManager$serve()

Story:
A event fearlessManager starts.
B fact No folder is at the 'manager path'.
C action fearlessManager creates the ManagerFolder at the 'manager path', with the LockFile no_manager.lock, projects.info holding Infos.list() serialized, and the empty folders icons and locks
D action fearlessManager takes the lock of no_manager.lock
E action fearlessManager$serve()

Story:
A event fearlessManager starts.
B fact No folder is at the 'manager path'.
C event Another process creates a folder at the 'manager path' before fearlessManager creates the ManagerFolder.
D action fearlessManager ends.

Story:
A event fearlessManager starts.
B fact In the folder at the 'manager path', another process holds the lock of no_manager.lock.
C action fearlessManager waits a little, then goes on as if fearlessManager started at that moment

Story:
A event fearlessManager starts.
B fact A folder is at the 'manager path', and no file of that folder has a name of form LockFile.
C action fearlessManager creates no_manager.lock in that folder, with the lock of no_manager.lock already taken
D action fearlessManager$serve()

Story:
A event fearlessManager starts.
B fact In the folder at the 'manager path', another process holds the lock of a file with a name of form LockFile that is not no_manager.lock.
C action fearlessManager ends.

Implementation notes:
The 'manager path' is chosen by the implementation, and can differ between operating systems: each version of fearlessManager has its own ManagerFolder, and a copy of an installation is an independent installation with its own ManagerFolder.
The lock of a LockFile is the lock of FileChannel.tryLock: the OS releases the lock when the process ends, however the process ends, and the lock follows the file when the file is renamed.
fearlessManager finds that another process holds the lock by trying to take the lock: there is no separate check before taking the lock.
fearlessManager creates the ManagerFolder by filling a new folder next to the 'manager path', then renaming that new folder to the 'manager path': the rename fails when a folder is at the 'manager path' already.
fearlessManager creates no_manager.lock with the lock already taken by creating a file with another name, taking the lock of that file, then renaming that file to no_manager.lock: the rename fails when no_manager.lock exists already. A file that is created first and locked after can be deleted by another fearlessManager in between.
fearlessManager deletes a file with a name of form LockFile only while holding the lock of that file: on Linux a delete ignores the locks of other processes.
Only a fearlessManager renames a LockFile: a process that holds the lock of no_manager.lock can be any program, while a process that holds the lock of candidate_manager.lock is a fearlessManager that is starting.
The Port is in the name of the LockFile, not in the content: on Windows a process can not read a file that another process holds the lock of.
